    "faqs_ijrNcG": {
      "type": "faqs",
      "blocks": {
        "tab_content_pBhcBm": {
          "type": "tab_content",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What Is A Dog Vacuum Brush And How Does It Work?",
            "text": "<p>A dog vacuum brush is a grooming tool that combines brushing and vacuuming functions. It removes loose fur and debris from your dog's coat while suctioning the hair into a vacuum, reducing mess during grooming sessions. For example, the Oneisall Cozy C1 Grooming Vacuum Kit offers this functionality, efficiently collecting pet hair into its 2L vacuum container.</p>"
          }
        },
        "tab_content_JmK8jh": {
          "type": "tab_content",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What Are The Benefits Of Using Professional Dog Clippers?",
            "text": "<p>Professional dog clippers provide a more efficient and precise grooming experience compared to standard clippers. They are designed to handle various coat types and lengths, ensuring a smooth and even cut.  Cozy C1 includes precision clippers suitable for expert trimming, allowing pet owners to achieve professional-quality grooming at home.</p>"
          }
        },
        "tab_content_c6HcW7": {
          "type": "tab_content",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can Professional Dog Clippers Be Used On All Breeds?",
            "text": "<p>When selecting a dog vacuum brush, consider your dog's coat type, size, and sensitivity to noise. Look for brushes with adjustable suction levels and appropriate attachments for different coat lengths.  Cozy C1 operates at a noise level of approximately 60 dB, minimizing auditory stress for pets and fostering a serene grooming experience.</p>"
          }
        },
        "tab_content_Kzi7Uh": {
          "type": "tab_content",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How Often Should I Use A Dog Vacuum Brush On My Pet?",
            "text": "<p>The frequency of using a dog vacuum brush depends on your dog's breed, coat length, and shedding patterns. For most dogs, grooming sessions 1-2 times per week are sufficient to maintain a healthy coat and reduce shedding. Using tools like  Cozy C1 can help keep your home cleaner by efficiently collecting loose fur.</p>"
          }
        },
        "tab_content_RK8XUk": {
          "type": "tab_content",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What Features Should I Look For In A Dog Vacuum Brush?",
            "text": "<p>When choosing a dog vacuum brush, consider features such as adjustable suction power, noise level, ease of cleaning, and compatibility with your dog's coat type.  Cozy C1 offers powerful suction capabilities and operates quietly, ensuring a stress-free grooming experience for both pets and owners.</p>"
          }
        }
